@* _Imports.razor (PROJECT ROOT) — Phase 0 error-fix pass.
   Blazor's _Imports.razor is HIERARCHICAL: it only applies to the folder
   it lives in AND that folder's subfolders. The pre-existing
   Components/_Imports.razor covers Components/ + its subfolders (Layout/,
   Pages/, etc.), but it does NOT cover sibling folders like Authorization/,
   Hubs/, or Services/.

   Effect: any razor file outside Components/ couldn't resolve <AuthorizeView>,
   <Radzen*>, the Roles static class, or any other namespace imported only by
   Components/_Imports.razor. This file fixes that by re-declaring the same
   imports at the PROJECT ROOT so they apply to EVERY razor file in the WebUI
   project, regardless of which subfolder it lives in.

   (The Components/_Imports.razor file is kept as-is — having both is harmless
   because Blazor unions the imports. Keeping the Components/ copy means the
   default Blazor template convention is preserved for tooling that expects it
   to exist there.) *@

